# Code owners must have WRITE access to this repository. A code owner with read or
# triage access is silently not assigned, and GitHub's linter reports
# "Unknown owner: make sure @user exists and has write access".
#
# Multiple owners on a line is an OR, not an AND: an approval from ANY of them
# satisfies a "require review from Code Owners" rule. Listing both of us is what makes
# that rule satisfiable at all — a PR author cannot approve their own PR, so a path
# owned solely by its author could never clear code-owner review.
#
# The two-person rule comes from branch protection ("require approvals: 1"), not from
# this file.

*                               @FreddyDezmal @Hanrekoen

# Highest-criticality paths. Both own them so either can review the other's work. The
# per-path entries document why these need care, and become real narrowing when a third
# person joins.
#
# verification-engine sends requests at live systems.
# security-core runs inside customers' production request paths.
# workflows are the release pipeline — the highest-value target in this repo.
